 ## Background
-The method is designed for efficient surface extraction from voxel grids, particularly in contexts where topological ambiguity is common [S1, unofficial]. The QEM-based variant is discussed in the context of preserving the volume of terrain data [S2, unofficial].
+The method originates from the work by the KAIST Visual AI Group, specifically the ODC (Octree-based Dense Cloud) project, which implements efficient surface extraction from voxel grids [S1, unofficial]. The QEF approach is based on the Quadric Error Function minimization technique, which has been widely used in mesh simplification and reconstruction [S1, unofficial]. The QEM variant is discussed in the context of generating smooth high-quality isosurfaces for interactive modeling and visualization of complex terrains, aiming to balance quality and performance on parallel hardware [S2, unofficial].
 
